# fixedbugs, defect 560, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R3; the
# ffi-pragmatist's `macro3`).
#
# One module's header defines a macro `twice(x)`, a hundredfold, and another
# module binds a `static inline twice` of `int`. `build` reads each header in
# its own module's unit and prints 300 and 8. Until 2026-10-10 `heroes test`
# read both in one unit, where the macro rewrote the other module's call,
# and the test below computed 400.
use fixedbugs560/int_twice
use fixedbugs560/macro_dbl

function main()
    print(macro_dbl.hundredfold(x: 3))
    print(int_twice.doubled(x: 4))

test "the other module's twice doubles"
    assert int_twice.doubled(x: 4) == 8
